  "body": "#705 (#692 step 1) has merged; this is step 2.\n\n## What changed (step 2 of #692)\nEvery viewport picker and the MCP pick tools now resolve through #705's one pick rule. No page carries its own pick logic.\n\n### The UI router: `crates/ui/src/feature_click.rs` (new)\n- It builds the `PickRay` from the camera, in perspective or ortho.\n- It converts the pixel radius to mm by depth.\n- It says which kinds the armed tool accepts:\n\n| Tool | Accepts |\n|---|---|\n| Plane row | faces only (#554) |\n| Axis by edge | edges |\n| Axis by two points | points |\n| Operation geometry | Face, Edge (with the face between edges) or Vertex mode |\n| Boundary | faces or edges |\n\n- **Hover** uses exactly the rule its click would.\n- **Origin/WCS chips** read the operation picks, so they get the same rule.\n\n### Removed from the UI\n- **`interact.rs`:** `pick_face`, `pick_edge`, `hover_feature_at`, `edge_nearest`, `point_seg_dist_px` and `feature_of_facet`. The old edge pick was screen-space, with no depth test, and offered facet seams. The file drops from 1779 to 1542 lines.\n- **`vertex_pick.rs`:** its local nearest/sight logic. It drops from 271 to 122 lines.\n\n### App side\n- **`pick/feature_sel.rs` (new):** maps a pick to the `FeatureSel` the pages store (`Chain`, run or `Segment`). `check_pickable` refuses a pick by id that a click could never make.\n- **MCP `list_features`:** now lists only feature-edge chains and feature points.\n- **Graph cache:** cached per facet allocation, so hover never re-hashes a mesh.\n- **Occlusion:** capped at 32 sight rays per candidate tier, a choice measured on `sample_ap214`.\n\n### Intended behaviour changes (#692's rule)\n- Rim vertices of round holes and bosses are no longer pickable points.\n- Facet seams of smooth walls are no longer edges.\n- Hidden edges are no longer pickable.\n- In the feature modes, the stock-mesh hover triangle gives way to the feature highlight.\n\nThresholds and trade-offs are in `docs/decisions/692-pick-wire.md`.\n\n## Tested\n**New UI tests** (`egui_app::tests::one_pick_rule`, real egui_kittest clicks):\n- `a_click_on_a_flat_faces_diagonal_picks_the_face_never_an_edge`\n- `a_click_over_a_hidden_edge_takes_the_near_face_or_nothing_never_the_edge`\n- `a_box_corner_picks_as_a_point_where_points_are_taken`\n- `a_smooth_walls_facet_seam_is_no_edge`\n\n**New app tests** (`feature_pick_wire`, 4, plus an ignored timing lane):\n- `a_pick_resolves_to_the_selection_its_page_stores`\n- `the_per_depth_radius_holds_at_a_miss`\n- `the_shared_graph_cache_answers_the_same_allocation_without_rebuilding`\n- `a_pick_by_id_must_be_one_a_click_could_make`\n\n**New MCP test:** `mcp_pick::listed_chains_and_vertices_follow_the_one_pick_rule`.\n\n**Existing tests rewritten to the new rule:** `vertex_pick_tests` (3, same claims through the real State), `law_tests::feature_pick_tests`, and one `plane_face_pick` assertion.\n\n**Gate:**\n- ui: all binaries green (lib 427).\n- app: lib 103, `feature_pick` 7, `feature_pick_wire` 4, `pick` 9, `mcp_pick` 3, `mcp` 13, `vertex_pick` 4, `plane_align` 8, `plane_align_edges` 5, `axis_align` 10, `wcs_align` 5, `face_origin` 3, `feature` 18, `fixture_ux` 9, `probe_pick` 9, `mcp_setup` 4.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: ui lib+tests and the app lib are clean.\n\n**Timing** (release, 400 hover picks, 12 px radius):\n\n| Model | All kinds, mean | Edges+faces, mean |\n|---|---|---|\n| sample_ap214 (1.5k facets) | 32 µs | |\n| Synthetic 100k-facet cylinder | 2.8 ms | 2.8 ms |\n\n## Not exercised / not done\n- **Fixture locate (#566):** wired through `feature_click` (merged with main).\n- **Pick-through toggle:** not added. `through: false` is set everywhere, and the API keeps the field.\n- **Others still owed:**\n  - round-edge centres have no `FeatureSel` variant yet;\n  - the WCS anchor markers are still overlay picks;\n  - the user-docs note for #688 isn't written.\n- **Hand check:** passed 2026-11-10 (user, builds of 47a33610 and e5d3b32e): whole faces, whole chains, corner points, no seams; both two-point markers show after the fix.\n\nChangelog: Picking follows one rule everywhere: whole faces, real feature edges and corner points only, the visible one under the cursor first - never a tessellation edge or a hidden edge through the part (#692)\n\nRefs #692\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n\n",
